    <string name="catch_switch">Will I catch it?</string>
    <string name="catch_switch_hint">Walking time to your stop, from your location on this phone</string>
    <string name="catch_timetable_switch">Alert on timetable times too</string>
    <string name="catch_timetable_hint">Off: leave-now alerts only when the bus\'s real position is known</string>
    <string name="catch_location_needed">Allow precise location so the walking time is right.</string>
    <string name="location_background_needed">Automatic mode needs location “Allow all the time”, or it works only while the app is open.</string>
    <string name="location_background_title">Location in the background</string>
    <string name="location_background_disclosure">Plan&amp;Ride collects location data to show “Will I catch it?” and to mark where your bus is in Automatic mode, even when the app is closed or not in use. This happens only while you follow a bus, with a notification shown the whole time.

“Allow all the time” lets this work for regular rides that start by themselves. Your location stays on this phone and is never sent or shared.

On the next screen, choose “Allow all the time”.</string>
